{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nThe authenticated-authorship merge-gate (`verify-identity`) is live but ADVISORY: `identity.require_authenticated=false` and the store holds 0 signed events. To make the gate actually enforce, write-signing must be rolled out first.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Write-signing enabled and producing signed events.\n- [ ] `identity.require_authenticated` flipped on with the grandfather boundary intact.\n- [ ] `verify-identity` enforces on new unsigned/forged events and passes on signed ones.\n- [ ] Configure self-identity + `identity.signing_key` on the write paths so new events are signed.\n- [ ] Confirm new events verify (`rebar verify-identity` shows `verified` for post-boundary events).\n- [ ] Flip `identity.require_authenticated=true` in the SAME change that enables signing (historical events already grandfathered by `identity.enforce_since`).\n- [ ] Depends on the perf fix (1cc0) so the enforcing gate is fast enough for CI."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785007210424375001,"uuid":"51836d8a-6a42-4c5c-8562-dc4ba01d2e26"}